I'd like to deidcate this ascension to my IPaq, trusty companion on all
my travels.  Most of this tourist was played by me while I was a
tourist... in Washington, DC.  I actually reached the astral plane while
on my way home and saved to finish the game where I would be unlikely to
make any tap errors on the screen.

This is also my first time with the wishless conduct, and as you can see
from the dump, I had no lack of chances to break the conduct.  I
actually got a throne wish in a random throneroom at one point and
confidently entered "nothing"  I finished with 11 total wand wishes
(including wrested) and 3 magic lamps.  I also went "oLS-less and left
with three.

I suffered from a lack of ?oID and had no few small un-id'ed items in
the bag.

I found three bones piles along the way that made the wishless conduct
easier.  The first was a wizard named Skeeve (Another Fine Myth fan out
there I see.) who's cloak was worn from that time on.  Below minetown,
was another named X, and I coudn't figure out what class he was except
that he had magicbane and some boots that turned out to be speed.  I
added those to my gear.  The final one was one of my own, a Samurai who
was petrified after a tap error on the PDA caused me to miss the message
about the cockatrice touching me.  His artifact weapon went into the
stash and was bagged for the run to astral.  His GoP replaced the
leather ones I had been using to that point.

I made careful use of my 35 starting darts, and left the 12 reamining
ones quivered for the duration after getting crowned just before the
quest.

Early on I found a marker, to be followed by two more so enchanting my
gear wouldn't be a problem.  I also found a magic whistle before the
minestair, so my pet was put to good use. Below minetown my dog Killer
was poly'ed into a bone devil and re-named Bones.  Bones allowed me to
switch from MB to the watch captain's saber.  He also was useful in
getting me some more money, although I did make sure to keep him away
from both Itzchak and the co-aligned minetown priest.  I ended up using
the sabre for the entire game, either two-weaponed with MB or Vorpy when
I needed more firepower.

I did a good job of keeping Bones around till he stepped on a polytrap
near the bottom of ghennom and ended up getting left behind as a killer
bee.

Some Oddities in this game:

The preists in Moloch's sanctum NEVER summoned anything.  I was saving
/oD charges because Rodney had been back three times already and I
didn't want to have to hack and slash him... the only spell I saw cast
in the sanctum was the pillar of fire.

The mysterious force hit me three times in a row on dl48, then seemed to
give up entirely.  I had to check to make sure I still had the AoY.

And finally after nailing pesty twice with orcus' wand I ended up
picking up not one but two more /oD on the same square just outside the
high temple of The Lady.  I left Astral with more /oD charges then when
I came in.


